## Proto File Structure

```protobuf
// pravah/pipeline/v1/pipeline.proto
syntax = "proto3";

package pravah.pipeline.v1;

option java_package = "io.pravah.proto.pipeline.v1";
option java_multiple_files = true;

import "google/protobuf/timestamp.proto";
import "pravah/common/v1/types.proto";

// Service definition
service PipelineService {
    // Unary RPC for simple request/response
    rpc GetPipeline(GetPipelineRequest) returns (GetPipelineResponse);
    
    // Server streaming for list operations
    rpc ListPipelines(ListPipelinesRequest) returns (stream Pipeline);
    
    // Bidirectional streaming for runner communication
    rpc RunnerStream(stream RunnerMessage) returns (stream ControlMessage);
}

// Request messages
message GetPipelineRequest {
    string pipeline_id = 1;
    // Include tenant_id in context/metadata, not in message
}

// Response messages
message GetPipelineResponse {
    Pipeline pipeline = 1;
}

// Domain messages
message Pipeline {
    string id = 1;
    string name = 2;
    PipelineStatus status = 3;
    google.protobuf.Timestamp created_at = 4;
    int32 version = 5;
}

enum PipelineStatus {
    PIPELINE_STATUS_UNSPECIFIED = 0;
    PIPELINE_STATUS_DRAFT = 1;
    PIPELINE_STATUS_ACTIVE = 2;
    PIPELINE_STATUS_ARCHIVED = 3;
}
```

## Proto Conventions

```protobuf
// ✅ Version in package
package pravah.pipeline.v1;

// ✅ UNSPECIFIED as first enum value
enum Status {
    STATUS_UNSPECIFIED = 0;
    STATUS_ACTIVE = 1;
}

// ✅ Use wrapper types for nullable fields
import "google/protobuf/wrappers.proto";
message Foo {
    google.protobuf.StringValue optional_name = 1;
}

// ❌ Don't use required (proto3 doesn't support it)
// ❌ Don't reuse field numbers after deletion
```

## Service Implementation

```java
@GrpcService
public class PipelineGrpcService extends PipelineServiceGrpc.PipelineServiceImplBase {
    
    private final PipelineService pipelineService;
    
    @Override
    public void getPipeline(GetPipelineRequest request, 
                           StreamObserver<GetPipelineResponse> observer) {
        try {
            // Extract tenant from gRPC context (set by interceptor)
            TenantId tenantId = TenantContext.current();
            
            Pipeline pipeline = pipelineService.getPipeline(
                PipelineId.of(request.getPipelineId()),
                tenantId
            );
            
            observer.onNext(toProto(pipeline));
            observer.onCompleted();
            
        } catch (PipelineNotFoundException e) {
            observer.onError(Status.NOT_FOUND
                .withDescription(e.getMessage())
                .asRuntimeException());
        } catch (Exception e) {
            log.error("Failed to get pipeline", e);
            observer.onError(Status.INTERNAL
                .withDescription("Internal error")
                .asRuntimeException());
        }
    }
}
```

## Error Handling

```java
// Map domain exceptions to gRPC status codes
Status.NOT_FOUND       → Resource not found
Status.INVALID_ARGUMENT → Validation error
Status.ALREADY_EXISTS  → Duplicate resource
Status.PERMISSION_DENIED → Auth/authz failure
Status.INTERNAL        → Unexpected errors (don't leak details)

// ✅ Include error details for debugging
observer.onError(Status.INVALID_ARGUMENT
    .withDescription("Name cannot be empty")
    .augmentDescription("field: name")
    .asRuntimeException());
```

## Bidirectional Streaming (Runner Protocol)

```java
@Override
public StreamObserver<RunnerMessage> runnerStream(StreamObserver<ControlMessage> responseObserver) {
    return new StreamObserver<>() {
        @Override
        public void onNext(RunnerMessage message) {
            switch (message.getMessageCase()) {
                case HEARTBEAT -> handleHeartbeat(message.getHeartbeat());
                case JOB_STATUS -> handleJobStatus(message.getJobStatus());
                case LOG_LINE -> handleLogLine(message.getLogLine());
            }
        }
        
        @Override
        public void onError(Throwable t) {
            log.error("Runner stream error", t);
            // Mark runner as SUSPECT
        }
        
        @Override
        public void onCompleted() {
            responseObserver.onCompleted();
        }
    };
}
```
